{"name":"Nuance","hex":"#e2e0d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nuance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A minor distinction.","Subtlety or fine detail."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply a nuance to; to change or redefine in a subtle way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nuance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nuance (American band)","blocks":[{"text":"Nuance was an American dance music/freestyle group. It was formed by the producer and arranger Ron Dean Miller, and featured Vikki Love on vocals. They charted three hits on the US Billboard Hot Dance Music/Club Play chart in the 1980s, including \"Loveride\", which hit number 1 in 1985. The same track peaked at number 59 on the UK Singles Chart in January 1985."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuance_(American_band)","wikidata":"Q7067801"},{"title":"Nuance (Canadian band)","blocks":[{"text":"Nuance was a Canadian rock band from Gatineau, Quebec, best known for their hit single \"Vivre dans la nuit\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuance_(Canadian_band)","wikidata":"Q28232959"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"nuance":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/En-us-nuance.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b0/En-us-nuance.ogg/En-us-nuance.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ac/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Simplificationalizer-nuance.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ac/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Simplificationalizer-nuance.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Simplificationalizer-nuance.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ac/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Simplif